# el-capitan

Route `crew <command>` triggers to the right crew member. If the message doesn't start with `crew`,
respond normally — no routing.

Known paths, never searched for: agents in `~/.cursor/agents/` (`crew-*.md`, personas
`<orchestrator>-<persona>.md`), skills in `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, tools in
`~/.agent/bin/`, task state in `~/.agent/tasks/<uuid>/` (resolve with `crew-resolve-task-dir.py`).

Lookups: follow `~/.cursor/agents/references/lookups.md` before you search for code whose file you do not already know, or rely on a product or API fact.

## Routing table

| Trigger | Crew member |
|---|---|
| `crew spec` issue/URL/description | crew-specwriter |
| `crew implement` | crew-implement → @crew-builder |
| `crew commit` | crew-commit |
| `crew open pr` | crew-open-pr — an open PR marks the task DONE |
| `crew review address` | crew-address-review skill — not crew-reviewer |
| `crew review` [PR #X \| spec \| idea \| changes \| (self)] | crew-reviewer — `changes`: staged; `idea`: proposal |
| `crew pr` view\|diff\|repo\|issue | `~/.agent/bin/crew-pr-actions.py`; writes stay `gh` |
| `crew resolve PR` #X or URL | crew-pr-resolver |
| `crew log` | crew-log |
| `crew memory` add text\|seed\|consolidate\|journal | crew-memory skill |
| `crew create issue` description | crew-create-issue |
| `crew evals` | crew-evals skill |
| `crew e2e` [PR\|status\|setup] | crew-e2e skill |
| `crew handoff` [resume] | crew-handoff skill |
| `crew ls` [--all] [--repo R] [--status S] | `~/.agent/bin/crew-ls.py --md [flags]`; `--json` adds issue, PRs, progress, activity |
| `crew report` [--since 30d] [--repo R] | `~/.agent/bin/crew-ls.py --report [flags]` |
| `crew doctor` | `~/.agent/bin/crew-doctor.py` |
| `crew gc` [--apply] | `~/.agent/bin/crew-task.py gc [--apply]`; dry run by default |
| `crew help` | `~/.agent/bin/crew-lint.py --commands`; print its table |
| `crew idp` | crew-idp skill (quarterly, not a stage) |

**This table is authoritative**: no judgment-call overrides.

## Dispatch

`crew spec` and `crew review` run inline only, because each dispatches its personas from the main
session. Everything else runs inline too, except two background workers: `crew implement` →
`crew-builder`; `crew resolve PR` → read-only `crew-pr-resolver`, given the worktree
`crew-worktree.py <branch>` prints; on its plan (its final message), read `crew-pr-resolver.md` from
Step 6 and `references/acting-on-threads.md`; follow them. Both dispatches follow the reliability
rules in `~/.cursor/skills/crew-implement/references/worker-dispatch.md`.

## Add-ons

Skills and agents under `~/.cursor/` that are regular files rather than symlinks are add-ons. Route to
one by matching the user's trigger to its `description` frontmatter, which names the trigger rather
than the implementation — an agent described as "Deploy the current branch to staging" is `crew
deploy`.

## Invariants

- `crew review` is pre-commit in `build`, advisory after the push in `respond`. Mid-iteration, ask
  an inline question or run one adversarial check.
- Every skill step that hands off names the next step and says "proceed immediately".
- Pipeline state, task resolution, and gate logic live in `crew-orchestrator.mdc`; the router only
  dispatches.
